   "source": [
    "Goal\n",
    "The goal of this analysis is to examine how stock returns and volatility evolve over time and across sectors, industries, and companies, and to leverage these insights to support informed investment decision-making and effective risk management.\n",
    "\n",
    "Objectives\n",
    "The key objectives of this study are to:\n",
    "•\tEvaluate market volatility trends across monthly and yearly periods \n",
    "•\tMeasure and compare average returns over time \n",
    "•\tAnalyse monthly versus yearly return patterns to identify seasonality \n",
    "•\tDetermine average returns and volatility across sectors, industries, and individual companies \n",
    "•\tExplore the relationship between risk and return at the sector level \n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Data Cleaning and Preparation\n",
    "The dataset was thoroughly examined to ensure accuracy, consistency, and suitability for analysis.\n",
    "•\tThe data was reviewed for missing values, inconsistencies, and structural issues across rows and columns \n",
    "•\tAll variables were checked, and data types were validated and corrected where necessary \n",
    "•\tThe Date column was converted from an object format to a proper DateTime format to enable time-series analysis \n",
    "•\tIrrelevant or redundant variables, including Daily_Return, Weekly_Return, Monthly_Return, SMA50, SMA200, and Volatility, were removed \n",
    "•\tNew features were engineered based on their analytical importance and contribution to the study objectives \n",
    "•   The dataset was sorted by Ticker and Date to ensure a logical chronological sequence, facilitating accurate time-based analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Data Analysis\n",
    "Monthly Returns and Volatility\n",
    "•\tReturns were calculated using closing prices and grouped by ticker \n",
    "•\tTime-based features (month, month name, year) were extracted and organized chronologically \n",
    "•\tAverage monthly returns and volatility were computed \n",
    "Key Insights:\n",
    "•\tJune recorded the lowest volatility, indicating relative market stability \n",
    "•\tOctober exhibited the highest volatility, suggesting increased uncertainty \n",
    "•\tSeptember showed negative average returns, consistent with known market seasonality \n",
    "•\tNovember recorded the highest average returns, indicating strong performance \n",
    "\n",
    "Yearly Returns and Volatility\n",
    "•\tYearly trends in returns and volatility were analyzed over the 50-year period \n",
    "Key Insights:\n",
    "•\tSignificant declines in returns were observed during: \n",
    "1.\t1970–1980 \n",
    "2.\t2000–2010 \n",
    "3.\tEarly 2020s \n",
    "•\tThe period 2000–2010 recorded the highest volatility, indicating heightened market risk \n",
    "•\tElevated volatility was also observed during: \n",
    "1.\t1980–1990 \n",
    "2.\t2020 \n",
    "\n",
    "Monthly Return Patterns Across Years\n",
    "•\tA heatmap analysis revealed patterns in monthly performance across different years \n",
    "Key Insights:\n",
    "•\tAlthough September records the lowest average returns based on the heatmap analysis, there is no consistent pattern in monthly returns across different years, indicating that monthly performance varies significantly over time and does not follow a stable or predictable trend.\n",
    "\n",
    "Sector-Level Analysis\n",
    "•\tPerformance was analyzed across different sectors \n",
    "Key Insights:\n",
    "•\tThe Technology sector recorded the highest returns \n",
    "•\tThe Real Estate sector showed the lowest returns and highest risk (volatility) \n",
    "•\tThe Utilities sector demonstrated the lowest volatility, indicating stability \n",
    "•\tAcross sectors: \n",
    "1.\tNovember had the highest monthly returns \n",
    "2.\tSeptember had the lowest returns \n",
    "\n",
    "Risk vs Return by Sector\n",
    "•\tA comparative analysis of risk and return was conducted across sectors \n",
    "Key Insights:\n",
    "•\tReal Estate: Low return, high risk \n",
    "•\tTechnology: High return, high risk \n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Industry-Level Analysis\n",
    "•\tPerformance was further analyzed at the industry level \n",
    "Key Insights:\n",
    "•\tInternet Retail recorded the highest returns \n",
    "•\tTravel Services exhibited the highest risk (volatility) \n",
    "•\tSeptember consistently recorded the lowest returns across industries \n",
    "\n",
    "Company-Level Analysis\n",
    "•\tIndividual company performance was evaluated \n",
    "Key Insights:\n",
    "•\tBroadcom Inc. recorded the highest returns \n",
    "•\tRegeneron Pharmaceuticals, Inc. was identified as the most volatile (riskiest) company \n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Conclusion\n",
    "This comprehensive 50-year analysis of stock returns and volatility reveals several critical insights into market behaviour across time, sectors, industries, and individual companies.\n",
    "The findings highlight that market volatility and returns are dynamic and cyclical rather than constant. Certain periods (1970–1980, 2000–2010, and the early 2020s) were characterized by significant declines in returns and heightened volatility, reflecting periods of economic uncertainty. Monthly analysis further demonstrates the presence of seasonality, with September consistently underperforming and November showing strong positive returns. However, the absence of a stable monthly pattern across years suggests that short-term market movements remain unpredictable.\n",
    "Sector and industry analyses further demonstrate that risk and return are unevenly distributed across the market. High-growth areas such as the Technology sector deliver superior returns but with increased volatility, while sectors like Real Estate combine lower returns with higher risk, making them less attractive from a risk-adjusted perspective. Conversely, more stable sectors such as Utilities offer lower volatility, highlighting their role in risk mitigation.\n",
    "At a more granular level, differences across industries and companies emphasize the importance of selective investment strategies. For instance, industries like Internet Retail outperform significantly, while others such as Travel Services carry higher risk exposure. Similarly, companies such as Broadcom Inc. demonstrate strong return potential, whereas Regeneron Pharmaceuticals, Inc. reflects higher volatility.\n",
    "Overall, the analysis underscores the fundamental principle of the risk-return trade-off, where higher potential returns are often associated with increased risk. It also demonstrates that effective investment decision-making requires a combination of time-based analysis, sector diversification, and risk assessment.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  }
